            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of osteochondroma of the mandibular condyle in atypical facial pain: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>686-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteochondroma of the mandibular condyle is an uncommon condition which could clinically present with chronic pain symptoms. This report describes a case of chronic facial pain in a patient with this condition which was confirmed radiologically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
